//:: cases TC_CA_1_InhaleOuterSuppressesInner
//:: tools silicon
//:: verdict Fail

// TC-CA-1: Mutual inhale contradiction — cascade suppression.
//
// inhale x > 0 followed by inhale x < 0 makes the state contradictory.
// DetectDeadCode inserts a post-inhale refute false after EACH inhale:
//   - after inhale x > 0:  state = {x > 0}           — satisfiable → no warning
//   - after inhale x < 0:  state = {x > 0, x < 0}    — contradictory → deadBranch
//
// The outer if (x == 5) also fires deadBranch independently (state already false).
//
// Cascade: the inner if (x != 5) is inside the outer if body.  instrumentBody
// wraps the outer body with currentBlame.having(outerBlame).  The inner branch
// blame captures () => outerBlame.didFire.  When outerBlame fires first, the
// inner blame sees ancestorFired = true and is SUPPRESSED.
//
// Expected errors: 2 (post-inhale + outer if). Inner if: suppressed.
void f(int x) {
    inhale x > 0;
    inhale x < 0; // contradicts previous — post-inhale check fires here
    if (x == 5) { // outer dead — fires independently of the inhale check
        x = x - 1;
        if (x != 5) { // inner dead — suppressed because outer if already fired
            x = x + 2;
        }
    }
}
